NAME: Content week
OWNER: Content Studio
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Monday at 8:07 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Content week" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Content week · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Content week · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Content week · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Content week · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Content week · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Stop exception: if the stop file exists, the stop check above applies in full except for one action it doesn't forbid because it only removes a send: before you end the run, unschedule any post you scheduled in a posting tool that hasn't gone out, and list in the daily note anything you couldn't unschedule.
First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/content-studio/ for one of your items (not a news- one, which the newsletter routine handles) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-content-studio.md yet, act on it with the content-week skill (a consent yes: recompute the hash and mark that footage "cleared" in the consent log; a post yes: run the send gate (stop file absent, not test mode and config.json run is tommy, live_sends true, hash recomputed from the pending payload matching the decision's, id not in the sent keys) and only then post it once if a posting connection has been granted, otherwise hand Tommy the exact post; a no: record declined; a change: redraft once as a new item). Add every handled id and its outcome to the sent keys, so a no or a change is never read again. TMEC Command may already have nudged you to act in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), never post: write what you would have posted to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-content-studio/ and do it first.
Then use the content-week skill: log any new footage in /workspace/tmec-team/media/inbox/, ask Tommy for consent on what you want to use, plan the week, and draft up to 3 posts (each as its own item in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/content-studio/, in the item format: payload with TO, SEND, SUBJECT, MEDIA and TEXT, then the HASH). If there is no usable cleared footage and no AI piece worth making, write NO_CHANGE and say in the daily note what footage is missing.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/content-studio.md: footage logged, consent questions waiting, posts waiting, the calendar for the week, thin shots, anything blocked and why. Never post anything Tommy didn't approve.
